A||||0||la9||Another Muffler Option||||1||
Z||000000||la9||07-05-2000||12:49 PM||||I thought I'd post this in case someone wanted a quieter muffler option. I just installed a NAPA muffler part #18157. We went throught the NAPA book and it was the closest match they had in stock. They had one listed that was 13" long but it was a special order. So I went with the one I got. It is 15" long 10" tall and a single in/out that is 2". I cut the pipe off the stock muffler at the welds with a hacksaw and slid the old pipes into the new muffler. The tailpipe sticks about an 1" over too far but I'll get a 2" to 2" adapter and shorten the pipe a liitle. Everything went pretty smooth and I got to keep the factory stainless steel pipe all for a mere $27.99 plus the price of clamps. If anyone would like further details I would be glad to post them. I am perfectly happy with the results.||||reg||1
